2c10bffb (1468 1793404269729 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f351-2a") (src . "liveness: a client gives up on silence, a daemon keeps a working request alive\n\nA socket client waited on a clock: a request whose work ran past the\nbound was answered transport-unknown while the daemon was still\nworking on it, and a long export could not be told from a hung\ndaemon. The client now gives up on silence, not on time: it waits\nwhile bytes move (the answer's, or keepalive spaces) and answers\n(error transport-unknown (reason silent) (window W) (elapsed ms))\nonce nothing has arrived for the window since the last byte that\nmoved; a send that expires with nothing written is not-sent. The\nrequest may have been carried out and is never sent again.\n\nThe daemon writes one space every K on a version-2 connection whose\nrequest has reported progress since the last one: export-code per\nfile gathered, projected and written; import-code per file read and\ncaptured; a commit per intent applied; a fold per segment validated\nand per segment delivered, after the segment is judged. A keepalive\npending when the answer is ready is completed before the answer is\nwritten, under one absolute bound; the terminal traces that it waited\nand that the matching completion released it. A version-2 request's\nprogress count is the connection's: registered at zero before the\nrequest is published to the executor, dropped on every way out, and\nreclaimed by main from the\nDOWN of a connection killed without unwinding. The executor's\nassociation with its ticket is set before anything is asked and\ncleared on every branch, the refusal included, and the clearing is\nread back from the table and traced. No keepalive on a subscription,\nbefore acceptance or after. K is below W, and both are read from the\nenvironment only under injection.\n\nThe command line, the channel and the MCP shell read keepalives and\nsend envelope version 2; the stream client sends version 2 too, for\nthe window before its acceptance, held by the client. A daemon\nthat predates version 2 refuses the frame as malformed-envelope and\ncloses; on exactly that refusal, once, the same request goes again at\nversion 1 on a new connection. This daemon refuses a version-2 frame\nit cannot use with the version in the refusal, never retried. Core\nforwarding stays at version 1 until the next landing. The MCP shell\nanswers a silent daemon with the JSON-RPC error -32603 and a data\nobject naming the reason, window and elapsed time. A connection that\nconsumes a cached writer's DOWN on a non-terminal path says so in the\ntrace, at six sites through one helper.\n\nTwo timed primitives change: a receive allowance already spent raises\nthe expiry before any setsockopt, and SO_RCVTIMEO's EINVAL after the\npeer's close is tolerated for that option only; the read primitive\nrecomputes the remaining allowance on every retry, EINTR included.\nA fault pause is a scheduling point and not progress. code-project's\ncapture-import is exported and datum-project imports the library\nwithout it.\n\nTests: liveness.sc (41 rows: silence with and without keepalives, the\nversion-2 frames and the once-only retry, the pending keepalive's\norder, the refusal branch's association, a killed connection's count\nreclaimed, byte identity of version-1 answers and of the base tree's\nCLI, MCP server and review channel against this daemon and the\nbase's) and liveness-streams.sc (16 rows: the stream client's\nacceptance window, idling past the window from the acceptance, the\npartial-frame rule, no stub left alive after the run, read from a\ncollected process table by a literal prefix); the io-yield capture\nrow sized by a measured capture and its census of the progress\ntables' operations counting fifteen; the change-stream guard\ncomparing both daemons' traces with the executor lines left out and\ntheir triple checked per ticket; the MCP shell's envelope row\ncompared whole but for the version digit, with forged negatives;\nrows-baseline.txt carries the new and changed fixtures' lines.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 555))))
